00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,922
Why does gold often rise when markets panic?

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:08,445
Gold is one of the five commodities you can trade on Meme Street.

3
00:00:08,814 --> 00:00:12,465
In the real world, it's been a store of value for thousands of years.

4
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:20,111
Demand comes from investors looking for a safe haven, jewellery buyers, and central banks holding it in reserve.

5
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:26,022
When fear rises, many investors buy gold as a place to hide in rough times.

6
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:34,828
Unlike a company, gold has no earnings and no boss. Its price is supply and demand.

7
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:42,000
What can push it down? Rising interest rates, calm and confident markets, and big supply news.

8
00:00:42,348 --> 00:00:46,687
On Meme Street, data and headlines hit the news wire, and the price reacts.

